<h2> What is a Google Doodle?</h2>



<p> Google Doodle is special modifications to the Google logo temporarily made by Google to celebrate holidays, events, successes and people. The first Google Doodle was designed in 1998 to celebrate the Burning Man Festival. The first animated Doodle was made in memory of Isaac Newton in 2010, and the first interactive Doodle was designed for Pac-Man's 30th anniversary. [1] Google also includes the works of different designers on doodle designs. At <a href="http://www.google.com/doodles" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">http://www.google.com/doodles</a>, you can see all the works made for Google.</p>



